    "updated_at": "2026-03-10T14:08:27Z",
    "body": "I had conceptually modeled `Origin.from()` on `Observable.from()`. The hope was that we could define a somewhat generic mechanism for obtaining `Origin` objects from an extensible set of platform objects that might have a reasonable origin representation (`Window` objects have an origin, `MessageEvent` objects have an origin, etc). We could certainly make that a union type that enumerates all such platform objects, but the pattern `Observable` introduced seemed reasonable to reuse.\n\nIf I've screwed up the ways in which strings are recognized/converted, I'm quite happy to put up another patch to fix up. If the approach is more deeply flawed, I'd love to understand how. :)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
