    "updated_at": "2026-03-10T14:56:07Z",
    "body": "Observable.from() needs _any_ since it deals with things which can't be expressed using WebIDL, as far as I see. But what is the reason for not using well defined and consistent union with Origin.from()? I don't think Observable.from() should be used as an example for anything in general. We should try to use WebIDL whenever possible to not have inconsistency problems.\n\nBut the most obvious, web exposed difference is that toString() isn't called if a random object is passed to Origin.from(). And that feels like an odd inconsistency comparing to WebIDL unions.",
